# Docker sends this whole folder to the daemon before reading the Dockerfile.
# Everything listed here is either useless in an image or dangerous in one.

# 197MB of virtualenv built against this machine's paths. The image builds its
# own; if a COPY ever picked this up, imports would resolve to paths that do
# not exist in the container.
.venv

# Secrets. A file copied into a layer stays in that image forever - deleting it
# later only adds a layer that hides it, and anyone who pulls the image can read
# it back. The container gets its configuration from environment variables.
.env
.env.*

.git
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Working notes, not application code.
reference.py
*.md
!README.md